# Documentation Sync Discipline

- When code, conventions, build flow, API names, paths, or tooling assumptions change, update the affected tracked guidance in the same task.
- Primary sync targets are `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, future `.cursor/skills/`, compatibility notes, and any docs or TODOs that would otherwise become stale.
- Common triggers include allocator pattern changes, boot-sequence changes, renamed APIs, path or naming shifts, workflow changes, and build or MCP policy changes.
- Do not leave a known contradiction between code and tracked guidance for "later" if the current task already proved the doc is stale.
- Keep rules concise and enforceable. Put long human-facing context in `AGENTS.md` or docs instead of copying it into every rule.

## Example

- If a task changes the canonical build verification flow, update `AGENTS.md`, the relevant Cursor rule, and any affected TODO or compatibility doc in the same task.
